<title>UK: Amey says gets 175 mln stg tramlink contract.</title>
<headline>Amey says gets 175 mln stg tramlink contract.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>British construction firm Amey Plc said on Monday that it had been awarded a 175 million stg contract to construct the 28 km Croydon Tramlink system in a joint venture with construction group Robert McAlpine.  </p>
<p>The tramlink system would be a light rail network linking Wimbledon, Beckenham and New Addington with Central Croydon, Amey said in a statement.</p>
<p>Amey was recently awarded a contract to design, build, and operate the 120 km A1 autolink from the A1 through Teeside to Tyneside.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44-171-542 7717</p>
</text>
